				Paragraph:
					Content >>
						On the other hand, **Cooperativa Solvent, S. Coop. Ltda.**, Tax ID F-17482211, with registered address at Polígono de la Canya, unit 6, Olot (Girona), represented by Ms. Carme Vidal i Roca, chair of its Governing Board (hereinafter, “the Client”).
		Paragraph: Both parties mutually acknowledge that they have the legal capacity required to enter into this agreement and, to that end,
		Heading 2:
			Text: Recitals
		List:
			Marker: upper-roman
			List item:
				Paragraph: The Client is a renewable energy cooperative that wishes to renew its visual identity and its corporate website on the occasion of its tenth anniversary.
			List item:
				Paragraph: The Studio is professionally engaged in graphic and digital design and has the resources and experience required to carry out the commission.
			List item:
				Paragraph: Both parties wish to set the terms of the commission and therefore agree to enter into this contract under the clauses of section {number of: terms}, set out below
		Heading 2:
			Id: terms
			Text: Clauses
		Markdown:
			Id: clauses
			Number markers: decimal lower-alpha lower-roman
			Typography:
				Line breaking: balanced
			Content >>
				1. **Purpose.** The Studio undertakes to design and deliver to the Client a new visual identity and a corporate website, in accordance with the technical proposal of October 20, 2025, which forms part of this contract as Appendix {number of: annex-title}.

				2. **Scope of services.** The services comprise:

				   1. research into and assessment of the current identity, with interviews with ten cooperative members;
				   2. the design of the logo, color palette, typography and brand manual, which will include:
				      1. versions of the logo for light and dark backgrounds;
				      2. rules for use in print, on screen and on signage;
				   3. the design and layout of the website in five templates; and
				   4. delivery of the source files in open formats.

				3. **Deadlines.** The Studio will deliver the visual identity within six weeks of signing, and the website within a further eight weeks of approval of the identity. Deadlines will be suspended for as long as the Client does not provide the materials or approvals for which it is responsible.

				4. **Fees and payment terms.** The fees amount to 18,400 euros, plus applicable VAT, payable according to the schedule in Appendix {number of: annex-title} by bank transfer within thirty days of the date of each invoice. Late payment will accrue the statutory interest set for commercial transactions.

				5. **Obligations of the Studio.** The Studio will carry out the commission with due professional diligence, appoint a person responsible for the relationship with the Client and report regularly on the progress of the work.

				6. **Obligations of the Client.** The Client will provide the necessary texts, images and data, appoint a contact person with decision-making authority and give its approval or comments within ten business days of each delivery.

				7. **Intellectual property.** Upon full payment of the fees, the Studio assigns to the Client, exclusively and worldwide, the exploitation rights to the logo and the other elements of the identity. The Studio may mention the work in its portfolio, unless expressly requested otherwise.

				8. **Confidentiality.** Each party will keep secret any confidential information of the other to which it has access by reason of the contract and will not use it for any other purpose, during its term and for the following five years.

				9. **Changes and additional work.** Any change to the scope, deadlines or fees must be made in writing and signed by both parties. Any work not included in Appendix {number of: annex-title} will be quoted separately.

				10. **Term and termination.** The contract will remain in force until the delivery and acceptance of the last of the deliverables. Either party may terminate it for serious breach by the other, after written notice and fifteen days to remedy the breach.

				11. **Data protection.** Each party will process any personal data it accesses in accordance with the applicable regulations and solely to perform this contract. If the Studio accesses data of cooperative members, it will do so as data processor, under the corresponding agreement.

				12. **Governing law and jurisdiction.** This contract is governed by Spanish law. For any dispute, the parties submit to the courts of Olot, waiving any other jurisdiction that may apply to them.
